{
  "_comment": [
    "Every third-party file shipped in docs/vendor/, and where upstream it came from.",
    "",
    "The sha256 values here are a pin, not the proof. A hash committed to this repo",
    "only proves a file has not changed since someone wrote the hash down; it cannot",
    "prove the file is unmodified upstream, because whoever modified it could have",
    "written down the modified hash. So the check in",
    "features/artefact/provenance.feature downloads the named package from the npm",
    "registry on every run and compares bytes against that. The hashes below make a",
    "silent substitution of the local file fail loudly and immediately, before the",
    "download; they are the fast half of a two-part check.",
    "",
    "Note the one rename: the meshopt decoder ships under a .module.js name in a",
    "three.js addons directory, but it is meshoptimizer's own file, not three.js's",
    "bundled copy. The comparison is therefore by content and never by path."
  ],
  "packages": {
    "three@0.160.0": {
      "registry": "https://registry.npmjs.org/three/-/three-0.160.0.tgz",
      "licence": "MIT",
      "homepage": "https://threejs.org"
    },
